# Glossary & decision trees

## Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Burn-down** | Gradually eliminating warn-level backlog |
| **Boy-scout** | Leave touched code slightly better than you found it |
| **Merge-base** | Common ancestor of branch and target — diff ratchet reference |
| **Ratchet** | Gate that only blocks regression, not all legacy debt |
| **Universal rule** | Violations counted per file (complexity, size), not per line |
| **Control plane** | Small JSON state file orchestrators read for gate decisions |
| **Public API** | Published import surface between modules/contexts |
| **Waiver** | Explicit label/process to skip boy-scout for one PR |
| **Build contract** | Single `SPEC.md` per [`contract-format`](../references/spec/contract-format.md): §G…§B |
| **§ addressing** | `§V.2` / `§T.3` — unambiguous refs in SPEC + agent chat (not commits/product code) |
| **Sectioned ownership** | Each verb writes only its owned sections |
| **Right-size** | Ceremony scales to blast radius; typo ≠ full chain |
| **Backprop** | Bug → §B + prefer §V + test + fix in one commit |
| **Drift** | Code shape differs from contract (contract-check skill output) |
| **Deep module** | Small interface hiding large implementation complexity |
| **Folder blueprint** | Durable doc of repo layout: principles, path map, placement, naming, extension templates ([`folder-structure`](./folder-structure.mdc)) |
| **Wide event** | One structured log line per request with full context |
| **Auto-clarity** | Drop compression for safety-critical or ambiguous output |
| **Stacked PRs** | Chain of PRs each targeting the branch below; bottom → trunk; merge bottom-up ([`stacking-prs`](./stacking-prs.mdc)) |
| **Layer budget** | Per-stack-PR caps: ≤20 files / ≤300 lines target; 30 / 500 ceiling |

## Which lint gate when?

```
New greenfield package? → error level locally; no ratchet needed yet
Legacy package, active dev? → warn global + diff ratchet CI
Touching 1 file in legacy? → scoped lint --fix + ratchet preflight
Agent generating new code? → treat warn as error
```

## Which contract-mode skill when?

```
One-line / obvious local fix? → build only (right-size)
Fuzzy idea? → grill → contract NEW
Code exists, no contract? → contract DISTILL
Ready to implement? → build (after contract OK; name tests for §V)
Test failed / bug found? → contract-backprop → resume build
"Does code match spec?" → contract-check (read-only)
High blast-radius change? → code-review before build
Unsure of library behavior? → research → §R → then build
Green build, spare budget? → codebase-design deepening (one module)
Need sub-agent for lookup/fix? → delegation — not for rewriting SPEC
```

## Which subagent when?

```
Know the file path? → Builder (or main thread if trivial)
Need to find path? → Investigator
≤2 file surgical fix? → Builder
3+ files / feature? → build loop on main thread, not Builder
Review diff for bugs? → Compressed reviewer
Want design essay? → Full prose reviewer / architect
Writing the contract? → Main thread contract skill only
```

## Which layout / folder action when?

```
Unfamiliar repo / missing path map? → detect shape → read or draft folder blueprint (folder-structure rule + engineering ref)
Where does this new file go? → durable blueprint · else sibling convention · else AskQuestion
New top-level folder? → update blueprint in same change · or reject
Deepen a module? → stay inside map (/codebase-design · /improve-codebase-architecture)
Layer / ports question? → /clean-ddd-hexagonal + architecture rule · then map path via folder-structure
Automate path rules? → custom-validators + ci-taxonomy Structure
Backend “where does this go?” → /clean-ddd-hexagonal (layer) + folder blueprint (disk path)
```

## Which test level?

```
Logic with no I/O? → Unit
ORM/repository against DB? → Integration
Supplier HTTP contract? → Integration (mock or sandbox)
Checkout flow in browser? → E2E
Invariant added in backprop? → Unit or integration citing invariant ID
```

## Which communication mode?

```
Long session, many lookups? → concise full/ultra + delegation
PR review comment? → path:line one-liners (concise review shape)
Commit message? → Conventional Commits; subject ≤50 chars
Agent memory file too large? → compress .md / .txt (keep .original.md backup)
Security finding? → auto-clarity full prose
```

## Which branch / release step?

```
New feature work? → branch from `dev` (ship-setup / branching.mdc)
Stay linear? → rebase origin/dev — ⊥ merge commit for conflicts
Land feature? → PR → `dev` with Rebase and Merge
Multi-layer / >~20–30 files? → /stacking-prs (gh stack; bottom → `dev`)
QA / UAT? → promote same commits `dev` → `staging`
Production? → `staging` → `main` → Release Please Release PR
Hotfix? → from `main`, then merge down → staging → `dev`
Full diagrams / edge cases? → references/ship/release-lifecycle.md
```

